{
  "root_cause": "During compilation/attribute validation, zend_get_constant_ex() handles class-constant fetches like parent::CONST while the current class may not yet be linked. In that state, zend_class_entry uses a union where `parent` is not a zend_class_entry* but a zend_string* (`parent_name`). The code treated `scope->parent` as a class entry unconditionally, so `ce->constants_table` was accessed through an invalid pointer, corrupting the HashTable header/arData assumptions and triggering an out-of-bounds read in zend_hash_find_bucket().",
  "fix_approach": "1) Hardened zend_hash_find_bucket()/zend_hash_str_find_bucket()/zend_hash_index_find_bucket() to immediately bail out when called on uninitialized/packed/NULL arData tables, and added basic header sanity checks to reduce the chance of unsafe HT_HASH_EX negative-index reads if a HashTable header is invalid. 2) Fixed the real trigger in zend_get_constant_ex(): for `parent::...`, only use `scope->parent` directly when the class is linked (ZEND_ACC_LINKED). Otherwise resolve the parent via `zend_lookup_class_ex(scope->parent_name, ..., ZEND_FETCH_CLASS_NO_AUTOLOAD)` so we don’t interpret a zend_string* as a zend_class_entry* during compilation.",
  "files_modified": [
    "Zend/zend_hash.c",
    "Zend/zend_constants.c"
  ],
